      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-09-01_WidnesExaminer_art0006" n="art0006">
        <p>AN ENGLISHMAN'S HOUSE IS HIS CASTLE or, properly speaking. ought to be. This can never be the case, if unfortunately a would-be householder has to resort to the Easy Payment System, a new name for the ini• quitous Hire System. To furnish a house on the Hire System. alias the Easy Payment System, is to establish and s,upport what is the most cruel, arbitrary extortion ever invented. The prices charged for the goods are enormous, without any regard for quality, the agreements are one-sided, being drawn with a cuteness which would do credit to a money lender, full of despotic and arbitrary restrictions, suchas not to remove the mark on the furniture, not to remove the furniture, not to wear the furniture. At all times to allow the mem&lt; naries to inspect the furniture. To pay the instal- ments regularly, and if one is missed to forfeit the furniture and all the moneys you may have paid, that is to say, although you might have paid £l9 on £2O worth of furniture, but missed the last payment by a single day, the vultures could empty your house and stick to the £l9 paid, as well as the iurniture. Other conditions such as permission to break open forcibly night or day, the outer and inner doors of your house, in order to take away the goods, and above all, that no matter how badly and wickedly they may treat you that you undertake not to resort to legal proceedings. Be warned in time, have nothing to do with easy payment or hire system. If you require assistanze go to Mr. W. H. Worsley, "The Pantheon," Gaythorne, Manchester, the largest House Fur- nisher in the North, who will treat you with consideration, sell you goods at the lowest cash price, and, if required, allow you time to pay for them, charging you 10 per cent over Invoice price for the convenience.</p>
        <p>For instance Mr. Worsley has several HOUSES OF FUR- NITURE on view at £l5 155., £2O, £25, £3O. £5O. £lOO, all at the lowest cash price, and not a penny less. Any of the above supplied subject to credit, upon 10 per cent being added to the amount. Particulars post free. GREAT BARGAINS AT WORSLEY'S.—DRAWING- ROOM SUITE complete, solid walnut, cost £4O, price for quick sale £9 cash. £9 18s. credit. with Cabinet, 2 Tables, Overmantle, Carpet, Fender, and Brasses, &amp;c.</p>
        <p>Heavy Dining-room Suite, oomplete, in Mahogany, uphol- stered in Ottoman Cloth, cost £4O new, the whole lot for £ll 109., with Side Board, Dining Table, Overmantle, and Coal Vase to match; also a Persian Carpet and Hearthrug. Magnificent Bedroom Suite: Large size Wardrobe. plate- glass. Centre door, wings for hanging, Dressing Table, Wash- stand, Three chairs and Rail, polished satinwood, ten guineas complete with heavy brass Persian Bedstead, Curtains, Mat- tress, do., all to match. Ten per cent added for credit. Note the following bargain :—Complete House of Furniture' mainly second-hand. for £2O cash; £22 if by deferred pay- ments. Consists of a heavy sitting-room suite in leather, couch, two easy chairs and four single chairs, dining table, mahogany sideboard, Persian carpet and hearthrug, brass fender, brass fire appliances, cornice and curtains, and pictures. The kitchen has a substantial dresser, chairs, arm chair, rocking chair, table, fender and fireirons, hearthrug, oilcloth, Ito. The bedroom is furnished with bedroom suite, chairs and rail, chamber service, brass mounted bedstead, patent wire spring mattress, Shetland wool overlay, bolster and two pillows, carpet. and fender. The stairs and the landing are fitted with carpets, brass rods. ac. The hall or lobby is fitted with oilcloth, brass clip, three mats and a cocoa mat. The above forms the most eompact, convenient lot ever offered. Other iota, £25, £.30. £35, £4O, and £5O, eqoally cheap; particulars sent on application. Every article guaranteed for five years, ezettanged if net approved.</p>
        <p>WOESLEY'S " THE PANTHEON," GAYTHOEN, • MANCHEiSTEE. `'.• ' : Hours Of busitim 9 eau. to 7F.</p>
        <p>•,:!!</p>
