        <p>SCOTLAND. ORDINARY RETURN TICKETS issued during the period from the Ist May to 31st October, are available for two Caiender Months, by OWL or BEAR, but are not transferable. If mot used within the pre- scribed period they are cancelled.. No allowance made for tickets lost, mislaid, or not used. STEAM COMMUNICATION BETWEEN LIVERPOOL AND GLASGOW. CALLINIS AY GREENOCK The first-class full-pewered Screw Steamers OWL and BEAR are intended to sail from CLARRNOR DOCK (south-west side), Liverpool. as under, carrying goons and Passengers at terms stated in Sailing Bills, to be had from the Agents. SEPTEMBER, From From Princes Landing Clarence Dock. Stage prompt. OWL TUESDAY, 4th. 1 p.m 3-30 p.m. BRAR—.... THURSDAY. 6th, 2 p.m 430 p.m. 0WL................. SATURDAY, Bth, 4 p.m ORDINARY PAREll:—Cabln (including Steward's Fee) single. 12s. 6d. ; Return El ; Steerage. single,f3e. ; servants in cabin pay full fare. Children above two years, and under twelve , years of age half these fares. 1 Cheap Return Tickets (valid for 10 days) issued between Liverpool. Greenock, and Glasgow. Cabin, 15s. Steerage, Bs. AsEarrs :—G. and 3. Burns, 30, 3arnalca-st.. Glasgow, and 10, Bernard st., Leith; William Sinclair, Excise-buiklings, Greenock; 0. MACIVER &amp; CO. 64, and 65, Tower Buildings, Water-st.. Liverpool. • Offices of the Bridgewater Navigation Company, Linilted,and Old Quay Company, 41. Queen-it. and Water-st.. Mancbeci ter, or C. Madver, &amp; Co . Albert-square, Manchester.</p>
