        <p>"I HEAR friend Rudiger has got n'iarried to an Ita ian lady ?" B Yes, he went South to save Itis_lungs,_and has lost his heart." PATIENT —" Then, doctor, you do not feel any anxiety regarding my case ?" Doctor—" Not at all. If I did, °I would ask you to settle the bill at once." LADY :—" If you. really love me, prove it." He :—Willingly. This water here beside us is both cold ant deep. Jump in and see how quickly I'll bring-Siou out." ExpLaiNtD.—TlariV• : "I hear that Joe DOdgum is a great mimic. They. say he can take off any- thing." red : "That explains it. I couldn't imagine where my umbrella had gone." "Au, my little boy," said the condescending gentleman, "and what might your age be?" "It might be goin' on 40," returned the polite little boy, "but it ain't." "Is Bronson as forgetful as ever?" "More so. Why, that fellow has to look himself up in the _Directory every night before he goes home from business. Forgets his address." - THE Dark One—" Well, Mr. Town-Gilder said this Victorian style of dress was particularly becoming to me." The Light One—" Yes, he told me he thought it a Splendid dress to conceal defects." . . A RUNNING ACCol7NT.—Creditor : "Your account has been running • a long time, sir." Facetious Debtor : "Let it run, sir !—let it,run ! ..... It's very big, and that may bring it down a bit !" THE RULING PASSION. —Doctor (to miser) : "I can do nothing for you, sir; your case is hopeless." Miser: "Thank heaven! -I was afraid I should have a long doctor's bill to pay !" SHE, inquiringly: "Married yet ?" .He, bitterly: "No." She, bitingly: "How surprising !" He, suavely: "Engaged yet ?" She delightedly: "Yes." He, revengefully: "How surprising." THIN-HAIRED MAN—" What! a shilling for cutting Ty hair? That's outrageous !" Barber— " But, my dear sir, the hairs on your head are so far apart that I had to cut each one by itself." ROMANCE AND REALITY. Seely Inventor: "I've got an idea that's worth millions, sir !" Capitalist: "What do you want for it?" Seedy Inventor: "Five shillings, sir !" "Do you knoyv Mrs. Fergusson has pneumonia, and is not expected to live ?" "No ! How's that ?" " Well, she got her feet wet going round to find the place to buy a pair of goloshes.' MISTY. —The word "alchemist" ought to be accented (and very strongly) on the last syllable. There was more "mist" than anything else about the alchemist. He was always groping in the mist, and he always missed the object of his search. A PROMISING- LOOK- OUT. —A young woman once said to a friend, "I should like to marry an eneineer." "A civil engineer ?" asked her friend. "Oh, it would not matter much; I would soon make him civil." PrtotrD FATHER.—" My daughter is going to Court this season-41 her marrii.ge, you know." Elderly relative—" Dear dear Aliout her marriuge already! And he seemed such a`nice young man, too."</p>
