        <head>LICENSING SESSION S.</head>
        <p>LICENSING SESSION S.</p>
        <p>DARESBURY. *th -ese sessions were held on Tuesday at the Curt W , Daresbury. The magistrates present were: . Long (chairman), and Alderman neld. retiPerintendent J. Atherton submitted the following ' 1113°tt to the magistrates.—" Gentlemen, I have the ti:c:4..eur to submit my annual report with reference taijbe Conduct of licensed victuallers and beer re- in this division during the past year. There are sep"tonsed victuallers, I beerseller, and 4 others who of the premises, total 29, giving an average of 326 ha,Te Population to each license. No licensed victuallers d„" been proceeded against during the year, being a ticrease of on proceeded against ,and none convicted in , ape.preceding•year. No beersellers have been proceeded j'eaallist, none being proceeded against in the preceding Ite„rj_ 19 persons have been proceeded against for eoness during the year,lB of whom were convicted, tnPared with 24 persons proceeded against, and 21 of ,victed during the preceding year; being a decrease . Persons proceeded against and 3 persons convicted. aerhave the honour to he gentlemen, your obedient kailvant! John Atherton, superintendent." The Chair- -400 8a id that the Bench felt that the Superintendent's The rt Wag about as good as it could be, and they had of gratification of believing that the reduced number tc:onvictions of drunkenness brought before them, had Dartarisen from any want of attention or care on the the police staff. They were glad to notice the sed sobriety of the people in the division. Alder- i'h4l:lNeild said the report was very satisfactory. The lie7erintendent said there were no tresh applications for 4,14.1)2,e5• A transfer of a beer license was granted to Cat 4 Eaton, Friendley Brow, Sutton Oaks, from erine Eaton.</p>
