      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-09-01_WidnesExaminer_art0083" n="art0083">
        <head>ildkaia .-,--!:_f•'-''-;--.,`-i`%-,,.</head>
        <p>ildkaia .-,--!:_f•'-''-;--.,`-i`%-,,.</p>
        <p>MINOR CASES.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON BOROUGH POLICE COURT. MONDAY —Before Alderman Harrison (chairman), Messrs. S. Wright, and W. Pierpoint. A SLEEPER OUT —Sarah Hankinson was charged with beiiig a rogue and vagabond found sleeping in a closet in Bewsey-street without any visible means of subsist- ence.—P.C. Clough proved the case.—The magistrates discharged her on promising to leave the town. DRUNK AND DISORDERLY.—The following were dealt with for bting drurk and disorderly :—Richard War- burton,hawker, 1 Edelsten's-yard, in the Market-place on the 25th ult., 51. and costs ; William Riley, wire- worker, 3, Edelsren's-yard, at the same time and place, ss. ; William Curley, carter, 4, Jolley's-yard, in Friar's- lane, on the 25rh ult.. ss. and costs; Samuel Ashfield,</p>
        <p>BIRDS. iNIMALq AND FISH STUFFED, and mounted in Glass Cai,es of any design. HEADS and HORNS mounted also for Sale. Birds made into Hand Screens or Fire Screens. Dealer in British and Foreign Birds and Animals' Skins, Glass Shade, 'las' Heads. C••binets, Mora Boxes, Nets. Isc.. for Bnlt-rdy and Fgg Collectors —B. Coate. Naturalist and F. jet.. 21, Ranstiaw-street, tireepoel</p>
        <p>-FURS, SEALSKIN JACKETS AND FURS of every description CLEANED or 11E-DYED and ALTERED. FUR SKINS dr.issed and made up into rugs, Icc.—B COOKR. Manufacturing Furrier, 11, Upper Newing- ton. and 21, Renshaw-stroet, Liverpool. Established 20 years.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-09-01_WidnesExaminer_art0084" n="art0084">
        <p>.'i.0...':.::::!.,7,:•::.'1.:,;,-,•..:....:',:;..'-..‘-,:::•..i.:..::..-....,..:•,:,. ~., ..... .. •</p>
