        <p>An Odessa correspondent says that in the Volga province of Samara a most remarkable sect has just made its appearance, of which ,as far as is known, (fly women can be members. These sectaries make a point of what they call " self-crucifixion." They feed exclusively on grass • herbs, and berries, and subject their bodies to all kinds of ,self-imposed„ tortures. They are opposed to the institution of clergy and the worship of pictures. It is said that a large,, number of women are being attracted to this sect, and gladly become mem- bers, • , GRIMSBY FISHING APPRENTICES. 610 BOYS IMPRISONED. An appendix to the Government report gives the number of boys apprenticed to the Grimsby fishing trade by public and ether bodies from 1889 to 1893, showing that there were from Altrincham 1, Birken- head 34, Kirkdale 4, Knutsford 2, Liverpool 22, Salford 1, Stockp6r(lo,. Swinton 10, Warrington .2,- and West Derby 12.' During the same period' 610 boys were imprisoned at Grimsby for offences against indentures. 'IT may-also be said that homeliness is only skin- deep. ALL geniuses are egotists. It's a pity the rule doesn't work both ways. ADA : "I have begun ro read the latest novel." Ida: "How does it end ?" IT is,always,surprising how much deeper a hole is after one gets into it: AN ORIGINAL une misery or being called Imori to httke a spee;li 'was got over thus by noted' lingiish mathemmjcian : " gentlemen, a de.Sire oc o‘i.igivality prevents me from Baying that tit k is the pcoailcat moment of my life, ' and it doe,3, not ouectr to iou to say anything . •</p>
